/**
 * NUTRIENT ENGINE — Food Database
 *
 * Nutrition data: USDA FoodData Central (foundation, per 100g), generated by
 * the pipeline into usdaFoods.generated.js. Pricing: BLS Average Retail
 * Prices patched per-food via `BLS_OVERRIDES`; USDA-derived foods fall back
 * to category-baseline prices.
 *
 * The hand-curated block below is intentionally SMALL — only spices &
 * fermented foods. The USDA pipeline has no `spices`/`fermented` category
 * (those descriptions fall through to `supplement`), and these foods anchor
 * the anti-inflammatory scoring + chronic-inflammation health condition.
 * Everything else comes from USDA_FOODS — running `npm run pipeline`
 * regenerates that file, NOT this one.
 *
 * Nutrient key:
 *   p=protein(g) cal=calories f=totalFat(g) sf=satFat(g) mf=monoFat(g)
 *   chol=cholesterol(mg) carb=carbs(g) fib=fiber(g) sug=addedSugar(g)
 *   na=sodium(mg) k=potassium(mg) ca=calcium(%DV) fe=iron(%DV)
 *   vitA=vitA(%DV) vitC=vitC(%DV) vitD=vitD(%DV) vitE=vitE(%DV)
 *   vitK=vitK(%DV) vitB6=vitB6(%DV) vitB12=vitB12(%DV) folate=folate(%DV)
 *   zn=zinc(%DV) mg_=magnesium(%DV) se=selenium(%DV) omega3=omega3(g)
 *   micro=aggregate micronutrient density score (0-10)
 *
 * Price key ($ per serving):
 *   us=national avg, ne=northeast, mw=midwest, so=south, we=west
 *
 * hormoneM/hormoneF: nutrients this food provides that support
 *   male testosterone or female hormonal balance
 */

